  "term": "lycanthropy",
  "definition": "Lycanthropy is a historical term for the supposed transformation of a person into a wolf or other beast, especially in folklore and witchcraft beliefs. In older psychological writing, it was also discussed by some physicians as a mental disorder in which the affected person was thought to believe or appear to become such an animal.",
